# Normalise line endings to LF in the repository AND in the working tree.
#
# Without this, git converts LF->CRLF on checkout on Windows, which makes the sha256 pins in
# docs/VERIFIER_SHA256 fail in a fresh clone for reasons unrelated to tampering. V00 would
# then fail in every clean-room run. See docs/BLOCKERS.md B3.
#
# `eol=lf` forces LF in the working copy too, so the hash is stable across platforms.
* text=auto eol=lf

*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.npy binary
*.npz binary
*.pt  binary
*.pth binary
*.zip binary
*.pdf binary
